        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(ios): persist chat thinking selections",
        "body": "Closes #106278\n\n## What Problem This Solves\n\nFixes an issue where native iOS Chat users selecting a thinking level would see the local picker update while the gateway session kept its previous thinking state. The iOS transport inherited the shared protocol's unsupported default hook even though macOS already persisted the same selection.\n\nThe two Apple apps also independently built the same gateway chat and session request payloads. That duplication allowed routing fields, explicit-null handling, and timeout policy to drift between clients.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nMove platform-neutral chat/session request construction and session-target normalization into the existing shared `OpenClawChatUI` package. iOS and macOS now use one typed request contract while retaining their platform-owned connection, route-lease, lifecycle, logging, and UI behavior. iOS implements thinking persistence through that same canonical request path.\n\nRelated follow-up: #106148 / #106154 shared response decoding; this change completes the request side without merging the platform transports.\n\nAI-assisted: Codex implemented and reviewed this fix. No agent transcript included because public transcript publication was not approved.\n\n## User Impact\n\niOS thinking-level selections now persist to the selected gateway session and remain consistent across reloads and clients. Native Apple chat request encoding now has one tested source of truth, reducing future iOS/macOS protocol drift. No gateway protocol or platform connection-lifecycle behavior changes.\n\n## Evidence\n\n- `xcrun swiftc -parse` on every changed Swift source and test\n- SwiftFormat lint with `config/swiftformat`: 0 files require formatting\n- `git diff --check`\n- Blacksmith Testbox `tbx_01kxdjexpymcshg4bxqanywyet`: `pnpm native:i18n:check` and `pnpm check:changed` passed on head `4db480585d16`; linked run https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/actions/runs/29245037966\n- Shared request/routing tests cover explicit nulls, filters, attachments, agent selection, and timeout policy; iOS integration coverage proves thinking mutation uses the selected-agent target\n- Mandatory local and branch autoreviews: no accepted/actionable findings, latest completed confidence 0.90\n- Hosted macOS Swift tests and iOS build required before merge\n",
